    "lang": "c",
    "pr_title": "Remove CMS code out of algorithm implementations and remove key downgrades",
    "pr_body": "There were large quantities of CMS specific code in the (legacy) algorithm implementations. This is the wrong abstraction layer for this code. CMS uses algorithms, so it is reasonable for CMS to have some knowledge about those algorithms. But not the other way around.\r\n\r\nThis PR moves the CMS specific code out of the algorithms and into CMS. By doing so we can remove a number of deliberate key downgrades we were doing to get the tests to pass.\r\n\r\nFixes #12983",
    "pr_comments": [
        "multiple simple travis errors need fixing..\r\n(Missing end line at end of header)\r\n+ looks like a missing include.. https://travis-ci.com/github/openssl/openssl/jobs/396455038",
